The rule uses a fleet-level capacity lookahead: for each available robot it estimates how many duty hours the whole opened fleet can still supply before the horizon, accounting for maintenance resets, and then prefers choices that avoid capacity deficits while secondarily balancing loads and avoiding unnecessary maintenance when the current fleet is already sufficient. Near the end it also prioritizes exact duty-length fit to finish the horizon with minimal overshoot.

