The new rule uses a horizon-slack and readiness-gap heuristic: it estimates current-cycle versus full-horizon capacity, then prefers maintenance-refresh moves only when current capacity is insufficient, otherwise defers maintenance. Among available robots it penalizes choices that leave no other robot ready for the next duty, uses exact incremental variance to keep duty counts/hours balanced, and orders new robot types by capacity coverage, overshoot, and efficiency.

